cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Surface–air coupling passes for EnergyPlus 26.2.0: patches, scripts and results"
message: "If you use these patches, scripts or results, please cite the paper and this archive."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jung
    given-names: Wooyoung
    email: wooyoung@arizona.edu
    affiliation: "University of Arizona"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2746-4983"
repository-code: "https://github.com/humanbuildingsynergy/EnergyPlus-SurfaceAirCoupling"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 1.0.0
abstract: >-
  Research patches to EnergyPlus version 26.2.0 that add optional passes solving the surface heat
  balances, the zone air balance and the HVAC to agreement within each zone timestep, with the
  scripts and summary results of a study of the order of accuracy of the zone heat balance on
  simple models with exact or converged references and on 45 U.S. Department of Energy prototype
  building cases. Not affiliated with or endorsed by the U.S. Department of Energy or the
  EnergyPlus development team.
keywords:
  - building energy simulation
  - EnergyPlus
  - zone heat balance
  - order of accuracy
  - numerical verification
  - prototype buildings
